schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Legal Structures for Your Local Node
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    How to choose a legal wrapper (co-op, nonprofit, LLC, DAO-specific
    structure) for a local ReFi node so the entity, not individual members,
    holds liability. Walks through risk-sizing (low/medium/high), staying
    informal, cooperatives, 501(c)(3) nonprofits, LLCs, and DAO-specific
    wrappers (Wyoming DUNA, DAO LLC, Marshall Islands DAO LLC, Cayman
    Islands foundation), with 2026 costs, a decision path, three common
    mistakes, and where to get free help.
  audience: local-node organizers ready to hold funds, sign contracts, or run public events
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      protection vs. overhead — "over-wrapping too early" (e.g. a Cayman
      foundation for a $3,000 treasury) is named as one of the three
      mistakes that actually hurt people
  related_concepts:
    - Legal Wrapper
  related_resources:
    - Wyoming DUNA
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  public_use: requires-domain-review
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/legal-structures.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: >-
    High-risk trigger: legal/governance recommendations (Principle from
    skills/ingest and skills/capture-and-route). This is jurisdiction- and
    time-specific (2026 fee figures, a 2024-effective statute) guidance, not
    legal advice — see the paired public-use-boundary object (05-).

# assessed-but-excluded:
#   - The article's decision-path checklist and "Try This" risk-read
#     exercise were folded into the summary rather than split into a
#     separate implementation-record — they are reader prompts, not a
#     documented case.
#   - MIDAO (Marshall Islands) and the Cayman Islands foundation route were
#     not each given a standalone resource object — only the Wyoming DUNA,
#     flagged by the article itself as "the big one for regen nodes," was
#     lifted; the others are captured within the concept-lineage and
#     claim-evidence candidates' text instead, to avoid four near-duplicate
#     "offshore wrapper" resource stubs.
#   - Legal Nodes (cited source for general-partnership default liability)
#     was not lifted as its own source-system/resource object — it is used
#     here purely as a citation, not as a knowledge environment being
#     registered for reciprocity.
